# Technical Specifications: realkevbase.com

## Stack
- Backend: C# / .NET 10 Minimal APIs, Stripe SDK.
- Frontend: React + Material UI (MUI) SPA.

## Backend Rules (RealKevbase.Api)
- Organize endpoints logically in `Endpoints/` using route groups.
- Product models must distinguish `FulfillmentType.DigitalPdf` from `FulfillmentType.PhysicalMerch`.
- Process Stripe payment webhooks asynchronously; do not block HTTP responses.
- PDF download links must use Azure Blob Storage SAS presigned URLs valid for 24 hours.

## Frontend Rules (realkevbase-web)
- Use Material UI components (`Grid`, `Card`, `Drawer`) for the layout.
- Cart state must handle mixed orders (PDFs + Merch) seamlessly.

# Repository Intelligence (repo-intel)

This repository ships a deterministic local symbol index at `scripts/repo-intel.lua`
(Tree-sitter for C#/JS/JSX/Python, PageRank ranking, hash-incremental cache in
`.repo-intel/`). Use it to avoid re-reading files and burning tokens.

- At session start, before searching files manually:
  `lua scripts/repo-intel.lua overview`
- Before reading a large source file, look up the symbol first:
  `lua scripts/repo-intel.lua symbol <Name>`
  `lua scripts/repo-intel.lua deps <Name-or-Module>`
- For a token-budgeted architectural symbol map (default 1024 tokens):
  `lua scripts/repo-intel.lua map`
  `lua scripts/repo-intel.lua map --budget 800`
- After editing source files:
  `lua scripts/repo-intel.lua update`

Read commands auto-refresh only files whose content hash changed; add
`--no-refresh` to use the cache without touching the filesystem. If the cache or
grammars are missing, run `lua scripts/repo-intel.lua setup`.
